    overview: "The March 21 livestream opens with Chuck Norris death jokes, the Undertaker waiting in hell, a Sidekicks tribute, and the first Buster grief receipt. March Madness and Miller Lite loosen the room before the new Spider-Man: Brand New Day trailer gets a full first-watch reaction. The Amazing Fantasy 15 pose and bright suit earn praise; the motion blur, CGI weight, Hulkbuster decoy, Mark Ruffalo fatigue, and a possible Sony/Marvel split trigger the first real fight. Venom and Punisher become a proposed trilogy and a morality test, while Tom Holland, Tobey Maguire, and Andrew Garfield are compared against the chat's favorite franchise double standard: the hosts can love Scream and still call out bad writing. Dune 3 then arrives with Robert Pattinson looking like a hair-dyed Batman, and the Halloween lane turns into a Jamie Lee Curtis credibility autopsy. The hosts argue that Halloween became a career ATM while Donald Pleasence and Dr. Loomis carried the series' emotional continuity. Ryan Gosling gets a grounded Ghost Rider pitch; Project Hail Mary and Brendan Fraser's Mummy comeback bring hopeful blockbuster energy. An AI Bloodsport remake and Frank Dux's alleged true-story fraud become a remake-identity court. Scream's Neve Campbell future is followed by an apology-video sketch, and Hellraiser opens a serious Tales from the Box anthology route with Doug Bradley's Pinhead used sparingly. The FAM then supplies a drunk beer-chug story, dog-loss support, Challis money-shot jokes, Cobra Kai versus Best of the Best, Jamie Lee and Hollywood-elite receipts, Snyderverse speculation, Lee Cronin's Mummy, Bruce Campbell, Friday as anthology, Anakin versus Darth Maul, and an anonymous Katy Perry request answered by Loomis. Local audio, captions, and aligned ASR support every route; playback remains the authority.",
